@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy | D2DJobs";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] = "Read the D2DJobs privacy policy and how we handle user information.";
}

<div class="container py-5 legal-page">

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 30 September 2026</p>

    <p>
        D2DJobs respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle
        information when users visit our website.
    </p>

    <h3>Information We Collect</h3>

    <p>
        The free resume builder processes resume content in your browser. It does not upload that content.
        If you choose to save a draft, it is stored on your device until you clear it or remove the site's browser data.
        When users click the Apply button, they are redirected to the official company
        or job provider website.
    </p>

    <p>Optional resume service enquiries store the name, email, selected service, and notes you submit so our admin team can respond. Employer accounts store company details, contact email, a password hash, job submissions, campaign status, and invoices. Employer sign-in uses a secure session cookie. Contact us to request correction or deletion of your account or enquiry information.</p>

    <h3>How We Use Information</h3>

    <p>
        We use basic website usage information to improve job listings, search experience,
        website speed, content quality, and overall user experience.
    </p>

    <p>We keep a daily aggregate count of eligible public page requests. The analytics table stores the date and total count, not an individual page-view record, IP address or analytics cookie. Repeat visits and automated traffic may be included, so the count is not a reliable measure of unique people. Hosting and security logs may be handled separately by the web host under its own configuration and retention practices; contact us if you need the host's current details.</p>
    <h3>Essential Browser Storage</h3>
    <p>
        The saved-jobs feature uses a protected, essential cookie to remember listing identifiers in this browser for 180 days.
        Theme preference and an explicitly saved resume draft use local browser storage. Resume drafts remain on the device and are not
        sent to D2DJobs. You can remove these items by clearing saved jobs, clearing the resume draft, or deleting this site's browser data.
    </p>
    <h3>Advertisements and Cookies</h3>
    <p>
        D2DJobs may display third-party advertisements, including Google AdSense or another
        network configured by the site owner. When these advertisements are enabled and served:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Google and other third-party vendors use cookies to serve advertisements.</li>
        <li>Google's advertising cookies allow Google and its partners to personalize ads based on your previous visits to D2DJobs and other websites.</li>
        <li>Third-party vendors and advertising networks may place and read cookies on your browser, or use identifiers, web beacons, and IP addresses to collect information as a result of serving ads on this website.</li>
        <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising from Google by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You can also visit <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YourAdChoices</a>
        to opt out of personalized advertising from participating third-party vendors.
        Learn more about <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
        Advertising remains disabled in the application until the site owner confirms approval
        and the required consent setup in the protected site settings. That confirmation does not
        install a consent platform: the site owner must configure and verify the appropriate consent
        mechanism separately before enabling ads. Advertising approval and delivery depend on the external providers.
    </p>

    <h3>External Links</h3>

    <p>
        Our website may contain links to official company websites, job portals, or third-party
        platforms. D2DJobs is not responsible for the privacy practices or content of
        external websites.
    </p>

    <h3>Data Protection</h3>

    <p>
        We do not sell personal information. Since applications are completed on external
        official websites, users should review the privacy policies of those external platforms
        before submitting any personal information.
    </p>

    <h3>Contact</h3>

    <p>
        For privacy-related questions or requests to correct or delete employer-account or enquiry information,
        email <a href="mailto:contactsupport21@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20request">contactsupport21@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

</div>
